**Why this file, and why MIT.** This license covers the kit's own mechanism — its scripts
(`scripts/`), its process doctrine (`process/`), its skills and role docs (`.claude/`) — the parts
that stay recognizably the kit's rather than becoming your project's own content.

**It is MIT, specifically, because part of what ships here is not this kit's to relicense.** The
Dev skill set under `.claude/skills/` (`brainstorming`, `writing-plans`, `executing-plans`,
`subagent-driven-development`, `dispatching-parallel-agents`, `test-driven-development`,
`systematic-debugging`, `verification-before-completion`, `requesting-code-review`,
`receiving-code-review`, `finishing-a-development-branch`, `using-git-worktrees`, `using-skills`)
was adopted from `https://github.com/obra/superpowers`, itself MIT-licensed (Copyright (c) 2025
Jesse Vincent) — see `.claude/skills/README.md` § Provenance & licensing for the full record.
Carrying that set means carrying its license forward.

**This reason is conditional, and the condition is worth re-checking before assuming it still
holds.** If the Dev set is ever removed from this kit or fully replaced with kit-authored
material, the reason this file is MIT goes with it — the license choice should be reconsidered at
that point against whatever content remains, not left standing on a precondition that no longer
applies.

**What this license does NOT cover:** the scaffold content meant to be copied into, edited inside,
and eventually deleted from *your* project — see `LICENSE-CONTENT` for that.
